The native attention experiment instantiates PyTorch's installed CUTLASS
attention template with a smaller query tile. attention.py also contains an
experimental transcription of its softmax reduction order.
attention_special_kernel.cu specializes that same template with constant
dimensions and attention parameters, retaining real bias for padded inputs.
global_attention_kernel.cu instantiates FlashAttention templates pinned by
the installed Torch build, from revision
14c377950125c70b7a9dabf9c561fca53715ac7d. FlashAttention's BSD-3-Clause
license and author list are retained in global_attention_FLASH_LICENSE and
global_attention_FLASH_AUTHORS. Its header source remains in the ignored
checkout documented in README.md.
The optional rope_attention build generates private modified copies of those
same pinned PyTorch and FlashAttention headers to rotate Q/K during shared
staging. Generated copies retain their upstream notices under .research;
the same PyTorch, CUTLASS and FlashAttention licenses above apply.
The reduction/normalization build adapts the existing exact CUDA Welford
kernel in ../native/kernels/native_vector.cu, retaining its PyTorch attribution
in the generated source. Its original license is listed below.

PyTorch revision: 08187d9e0fba026dc8217405802ab5381dc88d90
PyTorch license: ../native/kernels/pytorch-LICENSE (BSD-3-Clause)
Corresponding CUTLASS revision: e05f953a5b3d38adc240df2ff928e0421c2abba3
CUTLASS license: cutlass-LICENSE (BSD-3-Clause, with upstream file exceptions)

The PyTorch and CUTLASS header source trees are not copied into this directory.
Builds use the installed PyTorch headers and a pinned, ignored CUTLASS checkout.
Keep these notices with any distributed build.

The optional FlashAttention CuTe probe uses upstream revision
eed1971f5132630dc296fe37601e834d4b57a248 from an ignored checkout which retains
its upstream BSD notices. The optional Marlin probe uses the ignored Apache-2.0
vLLM checkout documented in README.md. Neither checkout is vendored here.

The surrounding model adapters retain the repository's existing Apache-2.0
upstream notices. Original experimental code follows the repository license.

The optional Turbo-Lossless adaptation includes Apache-2.0 source from
revision 50b72e5520f93cc855f0bd3a0114a7eb97338588. Its retained license and
attribution are in turbo_LICENSE and turbo_NOTICE in this directory.

The optional nvCOMPDx ANS experiment adapts NVIDIA MathDx 26.06.1 examples.
Their Apache-2.0 license and notices are retained in nvcompdx_LICENSE and
nvcompdx_NOTICE. NVIDIA SDK headers and device libraries remain in the
ignored research directory under their original license and are not vendored.

The optional cutlass_geglu kernels adapt CUTLASS mainloop and epilogue visitor
integration from the same pinned revision. Their retained BSD-3-Clause license
and attribution are in cutlass_geglu_LICENSE and cutlass_geglu_NOTICE.
The optional query_shard attention build instantiates the installed PyTorch
attention templates with adjusted query-row bounds; the PyTorch and CUTLASS
notices above apply.

The optional norm_geglu prologue adapts the same exact PyTorch Welford
reduction. Its BSD license and attribution are in norm_geglu_LICENSE and
norm_geglu_NOTICE. The irregular_geglu tile experiment uses the same pinned
CUTLASS mainloop and accumulator layout, with license and attribution retained
in irregular_geglu_LICENSE and irregular_geglu_NOTICE.
